<title>LUXEMBOURG: EU cuts 1997/98 rice intervention price.</title>
<headline>EU cuts 1997/98 rice intervention price.</headline>
<dateline>LUXEMBOURG 1997-06-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>European Union farm ministers on Wednesday agreed a five percent cut in the intervention price for paddy rice to 333.45 ecus per tonne for the 1997/98 (September/August) season.</p>
<p>In addition the EU Farm Council, as part of next season's farm package, decided the level of compensatory amounts in the rice sector for the 2000/2001 season would be equivalent to those fixed for 1999/2000.</p>
<p>It also said the monthly payments to producers would be lowered to 2.00 ecus per tonne from 2.28 ecus.</p>
</text>
